> widen(v: u32, n: u32 in 5..8) = n == 8 ? v : ((v << (8 - n)) | (v >> (2*n - 8))) & 0xFF where v < 1 << n
> widen2(v: u32, n: u32 in 5..8) = ((v << (8 - n)) | (v >> (2*n - 8))) & 0xFF where v < 1 << n
> equiv widen widen2
widen and widen2 are equal on the domain of widen (exhaustive)
  domain: v in 0..255 by the where clause (1024 points enumerated)
> w16(v: u32, n: u32 in 5..8) = ((v << (8 - n)) | (v >> (2*n - 8))) & 0xFFFF where v < 1 << (n + 16)
> w16b(v: u32, n: u32 in 5..8) = ((v << (8 - n)) & 0xFFFF) | ((v >> (2*n - 8)) & 0xFFFF) where v < 1 << (n + 16)
> equiv w16 w16b
w16 and w16b are equal on the domain of w16 (proved by SAT: 1630 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts)
